            <ArticleTitle>Acute myocardical infarction due to delirium tremens.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>144</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 36-year-old patient with normal-appearing coronary arteries suffered an acute Q-wave myocardial infarction during acute alcohol withdrawal and delirium tremens. Sympathetic hyperactivity with coronary spasm and increased platelet reactivity are probably the underlying mechanisms.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2000 S. Karger AG, Basel</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
